data: {"text":"1. That the Applicant most respectfully submits that he apprehends arrest in connection with FIR No. 215/2026 dated"}

data: {"text":" 10.04.2026, registered at PS Gandhi Maidan, Patna, under Sections 318(4) and 336(3) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023."}

data: {"text":" The Applicant has not been arrested yet but apprehends his imminent arrest in the said"}

data: {"text":" case and hence seeks anticipatory bail from this Hon'ble Court.\n\n2. That"}

data: {"text":" the Applicant submits that he apprehends arrest in connection with FIR No. 215/2026 dated 10.04.2026 lodged at PS Gandhi Maidan, Patna, which has"}

data: {"text":" been registered based on a completely false and fabricated complaint by the de-facto complainant. The entire case"}

data: {"text":" is nothing but a result of a commercial business dispute between the parties which the complain"}

data: {"text":"ant is trying to convert into a criminal matter by misusing the process of law.\n\n3. That the Applicant respect"}

data: {"text":"fully submits that he is a businessman of good standing and reputation in the community with deep roots in society. The"}

data: {"text":" Applicant has no criminal antecedents whatsoever and has never been involved in any criminal activity throughout his life. The present FIR is the"}

data: {"text":" first time that the Applicant's name has been mentioned in any criminal case, which clearly demonstrates his clean"}

data: {"text":" record and law-abiding nature.\n\n4. That the Applicant undertakes before this Hon'ble Court that he shall cooperate fully with the investigation and shall not leave the territorial jurisdiction of the State"}

data: {"text":" of Bihar without prior permission of this Hon'ble Court. The Applicant is ready and willing to join the investigation whenever called"}

data: {"text":" upon by the investigating officer and shall not hamper or obstruct the investigation process in any manner"}

data: {"text":" whatsoever.\n\n5. That the Applicant submits that he has been falsely implicated in the present"}

data: {"text":" case due to a business dispute of purely civil nature. The complainant is trying to settle personal"}

data: {"text":" scores and extract undue advantage by misusing the criminal law machinery. The allegations made"}

data: {"text":" against the Applicant are completely baseless, motivated and without any substance or"}

data: {"text":" merit.\n\n6. That the dispute between the parties is essentially of a civil and commercial nature arising out of business"}

data: {"text":" transactions and the same should have been resolved through civil remedies available under law"}

data: {"text":". The complainant has deliberately chosen to file a criminal complaint to pressurize and"}

data: {"text":" harass the Applicant, which amounts to abuse of the process of law.\n\n7. That the Applicant has deep"}

data: {"text":" roots in the community and is a respected businessman who has been residing at the same address for several years. He has substantial"}

data: {"text":" business interests in Bihar and strong family ties in the locality. There is no possibility"}

data: {"text":" of the Applicant absconding or fleeing from justice as he has nowhere else to go and his"}

data: {"text":" entire life and livelihood is centered in Bihar.\n\n8. That the right"}

data: {"text":" to personal liberty is a fundamental right guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the same cannot be curt"}

data: {"text":"ailed except in accordance with the procedure established by law. The Hon'ble Supreme Court has consistently held that personal"}

data: {"text":" liberty is of paramount importance and pre-trial detention should be the exception rather than the rule.\n\n9. That the Hon'ble Supreme Court in"}

data: {"text":" the case of Sushila Aggarwal v. State (2020) 5 SCC 1 has laid down the conditions for granting anticipatory bail and held"}

data: {"text":" that the court must consider factors such as the nature and gravity of the accusation, ant"}

data: {"text":"ecedents of the applicant, possibility of the applicant fleeing from justice, and likelihood of the accused tampering with evidence or"}

data: {"text":" influencing witnesses.\n\n10. That custodial interrogation of the Applicant is not necessary in the present case as the Applicant is willing to join"}

data: {"text":" the investigation voluntarily and cooperate with the investigating authorities. The apprehension of the investigating officer regarding"}

data: {"text":" non-cooperation by the Applicant is unfounded as the Applicant has already expressed his willingness to appear before the investigating officer"}

data: {"text":" as and when required.\n\n11. That the investigation in the present case is pending and there is no material"}

data: {"text":" evidence against the Applicant to justify his custodial interrogation. The Applicant's arrest would serve"}

data: {"text":" no purpose other than causing unnecessary harassment and humiliation to him and his family members.\n\n12. That in"}

data: {"text":" the interest of justice and considering the facts and circumstances of the case, the Applicant humbly prays that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to grant anticipatory bail to the"}

data: {"text":" Applicant in the aforesaid FIR with appropriate conditions as this Hon"}

data: {"text":"'ble Court may deem fit and proper."}

